record pattern match on opaque type `YieldCurve` outside its defining module `Shoals.Curves`

Opacity closes the read side too, because `@opaque` closes construction and
inspection together and hiding the representation is the point. It is *not*
what defends the pillar order: a field-by-field rebuild has to pass back
through a producer, and the producer guard rejects it -- using `curve_pillars`
alone, the rebuild compiles and then fails with `pillar times must be strictly
increasing`. `curve_pillars` is the sanctioned reader and hands back the same
two tensors a record pattern bound; `tests/curves_bootstrap.ch` and
`tests/curves_bootstrap_schedule.ch` were moved onto it in the same change,
with every assertion unchanged.
